# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the op-fusion programme's four-card window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/fusion-1 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards
# are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head (sed -i 's/tp4-fusion-1/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file the image
# carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# LEANC2 (TIMED, WPH-2 lean write_packed, WPH): the CONTROL again (A2); eight live (concurrent8_steady) in the repeat pair of the ABAB, every boot a fresh reset. READ:
# c2_smoke_check clean (a lever arm also has its engaged line and no fell-back line), no stall; then PAIRED per round, never by unpaired medians: python3
# scripts/ci/w2ln_timing_compare.py pair <A container log> <B container log> --window steady --a-smoke <A smoke log> --b-smoke <B smoke log> for (LEANC1, LEANL1) and
# (LEANC2, LEANL2), and its floor subcommand over the two control logs; the texts equal (text_mismatches empty). write_packed reads every destination's addresses before and
# after every write and builds one mapper a value; the lean twin builds one mapper, captures the addresses at first sight and checks them once a round in the window, with
# the same uploads, copies, order and fence. Duration (estimate): 35 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-traffic
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,concurrent8_steady
